# Unity-generated folders (regenerated by the editor)
[Ll]ibrary/
[Tt]emp/
[Oo]bj/
[Bb]uild/
[Bb]uilds/
[Ll]ogs/
[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/

# Unity package lock is resolved by the editor; keep if you want reproducible
# bridge pins, ignore if you prefer the manifest ref to drive resolution.
# Packages/packages-lock.json

# Loombridge captures/reports are large + machine-specific; keep contract + design
# target under version control, ignore the heavy run artifacts.
.loombridge/captures/
.loombridge/reports/
.loombridge/replays/
.loombridge/backups/

# NOT ignored, on purpose: .loombridge/tests/ (the stamped Unity test results, their
# binding manifest, and the run log). `loombridge tests run` produces them and
# `loombridge verify` grades them OFFLINE, so committing them is what lets a reviewer,
# a CI job, or a later verify read the evidence without re-running a multi-minute
# editor. Ignoring this directory would make the results local-only, and a gate whose
# evidence never leaves one machine is not a gate. A guard test walks this file against
# the path constants, so an ignore rule added here fails the suite.

# Legacy: CLIs before the .loombridge/backups/ move dropped the update backup here.
ProjectSettings/LoombridgeInstall.json.bak

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
*.csproj
*.sln
